vpinos-core (1.1.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Portrait mode for a Table screen mounted in portrait.
  * VPinOS Configuration: new Table Screen Rotation setting (Off,
    90° Left, 90° Right). It rotates only the monitor assigned the Table
    role, using Hyprland's monitor transform in hyprland.conf.
  * Setup menu: new Console Rotation option (Normal, 90 Left, 90 Right),
    now item 1, with the other Setup items moving down one. It rotates
    the text console through fbcon, applies straight away, and is
    re-applied at every boot by the new vpinos-console-rotation.service
    and after a GPU driver switch. The setting is stored in
    /etc/vpinos/console-rotation, with a passwordless sudoers rule
    scoped to the new root helper.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:50:24 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * vpinos-config add Priority.B2S = 2 to the VPinballX.ini config for
    the switch from b2slegacy to b2s as the default plugin.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 17 Oct 2026 11:59:31 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Main menu: System Info (Debug) moves into a new Tools submenu.
  * Tools > VPX Editor: launches the VPX table editor (amd64 only),
    offering to install it from the VPinOS apt repo on first use, with a
    passwordless sudoers rule scoped to the new install helper.
  * vpinos-launch: new "x11" client, like "installer" (Xwayland DISPLAY,
    windowed Hyprland config) but for any app that needs X11.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:59:31 -0500

vpinos-core (1.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Depends on vpinos-platform and vpinos-kernel: the kernel and the
    NVIDIA driver (prebuilt modules) now come through apt too.
  * Update VPinOS runs two apt rounds (pins first, then kernel/driver) and
    allows the downgrades a deliberate driver rollback needs.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:10:42 -0500

